# Project: CanvasChat - AI Canvas & Ideas Partner

## General

- This is a Next.js TypeScript application with App Router.
- CanvasChat is an AI-powered canvas platform designed to help users chat, visualize ideas, and generate creative content on an interactive canvas.
- Use React for components development, prefer to use functional components.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Use Shadcn UI components.
- Use sonner for toast notifications.
- Use React Context for state management.
- Component names are in CamelCase.
- Use next-auth for authentication.
- Use Drizzle ORM for database operations.
- Use Supabase for backend services.
- Payment processing integrated for subscription plans (Lite and Professional).

## File Structure

- src/app/: Next.js App Router pages and API routes
  - (admin)/: Admin-only pages and functionality
  - (default)/: Default public pages (landing page, etc.)
  - (legal)/: Legal pages (privacy policy, terms, etc.)
  - api/: API routes for backend operations
  - auth/: Authentication-related pages
  - pay-success/: Payment success pages
  - yan/: Main CanvasChat application pages
  - globals.css, theme.css, yan.css: Global styles and theming
- src/auth/: Authentication configuration and handlers
- src/components/: React components
  - analytics/: Analytics and tracking components
  - blocks/: Layout blocks (header, footer, etc.), commonly used in Landing Page
  - console/: Admin console components
  - copyit/: Copy-to-clipboard functionality
  - dashboard/: Dashboard UI components
  - emails/: Email template components
  - feedback/: User feedback components
  - icon/: Custom icon components
  - invite/: User invitation components
  - locale/: Localization components
  - markdown/: Markdown rendering components
  - motion-primitives/: Animation and motion components
  - sign/: Sign-in/sign-up components
  - theme/: Theme switching components
  - ui/: Reusable UI components (Shadcn UI)
  - yan/: CanvasChat-specific components
- src/contexts/: React contexts for global state management
- src/db/: Database configuration and schema
  - migrations/: Database migration files
- src/hooks/: Custom React hooks
- src/lib/: Custom libraries and utility functions
  - chat-store/: Chat state management
  - aimodels.ts: AI model configurations
  - cache.ts: Caching utilities
  - config.ts: Application configuration
  - gateway.ts: API gateway utilities
  - supabase.ts: Supabase client configuration
- src/middleware.ts: Next.js middleware
- src/models/: Data models and data operations
- src/providers/: React providers (theme, etc.)
- src/services/: Business logic and external service integrations
- src/types/: TypeScript type definitions
  - blocks/: Types for layout blocks
  - pages/: Types for pages
  - slots/: Types for slot-based components
  - API and domain-specific type definitions
- public/: Static assets
  - imgs/: Image assets (icons, logos, masks, etc.)
  - favicon.ico, logo.png: Brand assets
  - robots.txt, sitemap.xml: SEO files
- docs/: Project documentation
- debug/: Development and debugging tools
- .env.development: Development environment variables

## Key Features

- AI-powered canvas for idea generation and visualization
- Multi-provider AI model support (OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Google)
- Credit-based system for AI conversations and features
- User authentication and profile management
- Real-time chat interface with AI agents
- Responsive design with dark/light theme support

## Coding Conventions

- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Follow React best practices and hooks
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind CSS and Shadcn UI
- Keep components modular and reusable
- Use proper type definitions for components and data
- Organize components by feature/domain in appropriate directories
- Use consistent naming conventions (CamelCase for components, kebab-case for files)
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions for routing and data fetching
- Use server components by default, client components only when necessary for interactivity
